<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jinshin War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">672</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jinshin War was a succession war fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 672 after the death of Emperor Tenji. Tenji's brother Prince Ōama raised forces in the eastern provinces and defeated the court of Tenji's son, Prince Ōtomo, who took his own life. The victor took the throne as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-tenmu">Emperor Tenmu</a> and used his strengthened position to build a centralised bureaucratic state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jinshin-war.jpg" alt="Jinshin War" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saigen Jiro · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omi_Otsu-no-miya,_dairi-seiden-ato.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
